<task label="vectors-coding-nearestPair">
    <statement>
        <p>
            Write a function <pf>nearestPair()</pf> that takes a vector <pf>v</pf> and returns the pair of values in <pf>v</pf> with the smallest absolute difference. If <pf>v</pf> has fewer than two elements, return <pf>[]</pf>. If more than one pair is tied for closest, return the first pair found. Use nested loops.
        </p>

        <tabular valign="top" top="minor">
            <col width="11%" halign="right" />
            <col width="15%" halign="left" />
            <col width="28%" halign="center" />
            <col width="46%" halign="left" />
            <row>
                <cell>Inputs:</cell>
                <cell><p><pf>v</pf></p></cell>
                <cell><p>(1xn) double</p></cell>
                <cell><p>vector of any length</p></cell>
            </row>
            <row bottom="minor">
                <cell>Outputs:</cell>
                <cell><p><pf>pair</pf></p></cell>
                <cell><p>(1x2) double</p></cell>
                <cell><p>closest pair of values in <pf>v</pf>, or <pf>[]</pf> if <pf>v</pf> has fewer than two elements</p></cell>
            </row>
        </tabular>

        <sidebyside widths="58% 40%">
            <stack>
                <p>Test Cases ⤵︎</p>
                <program language="matlab">
                    pair = nearestPair([10, 4, 22, 7, 5])
                    pair = nearestPair([100, 101, 250, 500])
                    pair = nearestPair([-3, 0, -3, -3, 3, 1])
                    pair = nearestPair([42])
                </program>
            </stack>
            <stack>
                <p>Expected ⤵︎</p>
                <program language="matlab">
                    pair = [4, 5]
                    pair = [100, 101]
                    pair = [-3, -3]
                    pair = []
                </program>
            </stack>
        </sidebyside>
    </statement>

    <solution component="exercise-solution">
        <p>
            Here is one possible solution. The outer loop chooses the first value in the pair, and the inner loop checks every later value against it.
        </p>
        <program language="matlab">
            function pair = nearestPair(v)
                if length(v) &lt; 2
                    pair = [];
                    return
                end

                pair = [v(1), v(2)];
                bestDist = abs(v(1) - v(2));

                for i = 1:(length(v) - 1)
                    for j = (i + 1):length(v)
                        d = abs(v(i) - v(j));
                        if d &lt; bestDist
                            bestDist = d;
                            pair = [v(i), v(j)];
                        end
                    end
                end
            end
        </program>
    </solution>
</task>